Z||000010||lou_dias||08-09-2001||09:10 AM||||I haven't posted there either and I stopped reading it weeks ago.<BR>I think the main problem here is that alot of guys here spend way too much time on their cars and not enough time socializing locally.  So when they come here to talk about their cars, it's just so fitting to kill 2 birds with one stone.<P>I've never met her and I don't post that much but I've been reading the forum for 1.5 years and from what I've gathered, she seems pretty down to earth.<P>Ofcourse from knowing many different people from all parts of the country, I would say she's typical of mid-western girls.  That's accually a compliment as I have found the Ohio Valley to have lots of down to earth girls.  Must be the upbringing or something.<P>Well, we are all products of our environment, right?  They women around here are kinda like the women in Cali.  Luckily the girl I'm currently dating is pretty cool.  That's not the norm around here.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Toddster||08-09-2001||01:18 PM||||WE ARE BACK!<P>We won the long distance trophy. Well earned too. It took 36 hours of driving to get home! over 6400 miles round trip.<P>The show was OK but the Ramada was awful. Not only were the rooms poor, the banquet was picnic food, and the staff terrible but at $94 a night it was way overpriced. My S.O. was a hotel manager and we were both amazed at how little we got for the money. Phil, we'll talk!<P>The show itself, was fun but I expected more cars. Williamsburg was such a central location. We only had about 100 cars.<P>The trip was HOT HOT HOT! I pulled a U-Haul Sport trailer and traveling across the desert, in August, up hills, put a load on the car. But it was worth it. For the first time I got to meet a lot of people I've only emailed, or read about.<P>Looking forward to next year.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000012||fierovette||08-09-2001||05:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Toddster:<BR><B>WE ARE BACK!<P>We won the long distance trophy. Well earned too. It took 36 hours of driving to get home! over 6400 miles round trip.<P>The show was OK but the Ramada was awful. Not only were the rooms poor, the banquet was picnic food, and the staff terrible but at $94 a night it was way overpriced. My S.O. was a hotel manager and we were both amazed at how little we got for the money. Phil, we'll talk!<P>The show itself, was fun but I expected more cars. Williamsburg was such a central location. We only had about 100 cars.<P>The trip was HOT HOT HOT! I pulled a U-Haul Sport trailer and traveling across the desert, in August, up hills, put a load on the car. But it was worth it. For the first time I got to meet a lot of people I've only emailed, or read about.<P>Looking forward to next year.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>You must be the one we stat next to at the banquet, Bill & Trish (fierovette) from CT.Glad to hear you made it back OK. <P>||||reg||1
